## 7. Privacy and sharing

The website should work without accounts or sign-in.

Keep journal responses in memory by default unless the user explicitly chooses to copy or share them. Do not silently upload personal messages, record microphone audio, or store sensitive responses on a server.

WhatsApp sharing must be user-initiated. If a recipient number is configured, keep it out of public source control where feasible and document the limitations of client-side configuration.

If the website is hosted publicly, do not assume that a public URL is private merely because it is unlisted.

